SUMMARY:Historical Society of Ottawa - Lest We Forget? An exploration of the Valour and Unequal Treatment of Algonquin who have served in Canada’s Armed Forces
DESCRIPTION:Guest Speaker\nLynn Gehl Ph.D\, Anishinaabe Algonquin Advocate\, Academic\, Author & Artist \nWendy Jocko Sgt. CD (Ret’d)\,  Former Chief of the Algonquins of Pikwakanagan First Nation. Canadian Forces Veteran \nDetails \nWendy Jocko’s uncle and four great uncles served in WWI and her father and five uncles served in WWII. Wendy served for 23 years\, including tours of duty in Bosnia and Croatia.\nWendy’s son served in the 1st Battalion of the Royal Canadian Regiment. \nIn Lynn Gehl’s book “Joseph Gagnon: An Algonquin World War I Veteran”\, she recounts the story of her great-grandfather who\, in exchange for his wartime service and sacrifices\, found himself stripped of his rights as an Indigenous person\, yet denied the rights accorded non-Indigenous veterans. \nThis presentation will take place on Zoom. All are welcome. Zoom registration link below.
URL:https://ontariohistoricalsociety.ca/event/historical-society-of-ottawa-lest-we-forget/
LOCATION:online
ORGANIZER;CN="The Historical Society of Ottawa":MAILTO:info@historicalsocietyottawa.ca
GEO:56.130366;-106.346771
END:VEVENT
