SUMMARY:Thornhill Historical Society - Speakers Event\, The Enigma of Grace Marks
DESCRIPTION:We are pleased to invite you to an upcoming Thornhill Historical Society Speakers Event\, The Enigma of Grace Marks. \nThe evening will explore the remarkable and mysterious story of Grace Marks\, the 19th-century Canadian woman whose life and notorious murder trial inspired acclaimed Canadian author Margaret Atwood to write the best-selling novel Alias Grace. \nWe hope you\, your friends\, and neighbours will join us for what promises to be a fascinating evening of Canadian history\, mystery and storytelling by expert presenter Jessica Allen. Refreshment and treats will be served at 7:15\, presentation starts at 7:30. \nRSVP by Wed. Oct. 14 to Valerie Burke programs@thornhillhistoric.org
URL:https://ontariohistoricalsociety.ca/event/thornhill-historical-society-speakers-event-the-enigma-of-grace-marks/
LOCATION:Heintzman House\, Bay Thorn Drive 135\, Markham\, Ontario\, L3T 3V1\, Canada
ORGANIZER;CN="Thornhill Heritage Society":MAILTO:president@thornhillhistoric.org
GEO:43.8238317;-79.4162569
