SUMMARY:Newcastle Village and District Historical Society Presentation: British Home Children in Clarington
DESCRIPTION:Mark your calendars! \nBritish Home Children in Clarington\nA Presentation by Sheila Dodd \nExplore the history and lives of the British Home Children who were placed in Clarington. Sheila Dodd will highlight the sending agencies\, receiving homes\, and the challenges many British Home Children faced once in Canada. \nFree admission \nAccredited speaker with Home Children Canada\, Sheila Dodd will be giving a brief history about the BHC child migration scheme and some of the sending agencies and receiving homes in the area. She will be focusing on children placed in the Clarington area and those that ended up living and dying here. By using new case studies\, Sheila hopes to bring some of these indentured servants and labourers stories to life and show the challenges that most British Home Children faced once in Canada. Over 100\,000 children were sent from Britain to Canada from 1869-1948 and is a forgotten part of Canadian history that Sheila and others helped to keep alive.
URL:https://ontariohistoricalsociety.ca/event/newcastle-village-and-district-historical-society-presentation-british-home-children-in-clarington/
LOCATION:Newcastle Community Hall\, 20 King Ave W.\, Newcastle\, Ontario\, L1B 1H7\, Canada
ORGANIZER;CN="Newcastle Village and District Historical Society":MAILTO:info@newcastlehistorical.ca
GEO:43.9175514;-78.5894004
