SUMMARY:Historical Society of Ottawa - Creating UNREST: A Fiction Writer’s Journey into Our Past
DESCRIPTION:Gwen Tuinman\, Author Unrest \nDetails\nA behind-the-scenes look at how Unrest\, set in 1836 Bytown\, grew from historical research into fiction. Gwen will share how primary and secondary sources\, from maps and essays to museum visits and walks in the woods\, helped her imagine the people who lived here and the world they inhabited. Gwen will also discuss how her Irish ancestry inspired the story\, the themes that emerged as she wrote\, and how Bytown’s history became the foundation for the novel. \nAdmission is free. All are welcome to attend. \n* Please note the special time & special venue. * \n 
URL:https://ontariohistoricalsociety.ca/event/historical-society-of-ottawa-unrest/
LOCATION:Ottawa Public Library\, St-Laurent Branch\, Coté Street 515\, Ottawa\, Ontario\, K1K 0Z8\, Canada
ORGANIZER;CN="The Historical Society of Ottawa":MAILTO:info@historicalsocietyottawa.ca
GEO:45.4362488;-75.6477027
